  "scene": {
    "id": "S3-agentfactory",
    "title": "Option 3 hypothesis · Agent Factory (AgentAiR)",
    "caption": "Hypothesis drawn on the AgentAiR overview draw.io, zoning kept: 85BB PCP-GCP ⊃ 4AE9 AI Platform ⊃ 7EFD Everyday AI (Agent\nFactory model: Gemini Enterprise; Agent Platform with Agent Gateway (IAP), Policies, Model Armor, Agent Registry / Runtime), C9EC Datahub\nand the platform cells (logging, connectivity, Model Armor floor, VPC SC, governed APIs, IAM/PAB); links follow the draw.io relations.\nHRPN adds its ADK `root_agent` (already wrapped as `AdkApp`) registered on Agent Runtime, its tools, and an AAI HR spoke project with\nRAG Engine, documents bucket and Drive sync (ARB slide 7 hub-and-spoke, slide 9 \"Agent Factory · AAI HR instance\").\nGoogle Chat is NOT the channel here: users reach the agent in the Gemini Enterprise app, so BRD-HR-010 (Chat, mandatory) needs a waiver.\nRed frames: Agent Engine POD-only, not in the production landing zone (HR master ARD note 2026-02-27, to recheck); Gemini Enterprise\nplanned Q4 2026, not SEC4AI-assessed; Agent Runtime under VPC-SC needs `min_instances` ≥ 1; PSL spoke template end 2026, retrofit required.\nFeasibility precedent outside Airbus: ADK agent on Agent Runtime registered in Gemini Enterprise Business with a cross-project IAM grant.\nDelivery (hypothesis): the ADK code keeps its GenAiR-Cutter / AgentGarden origin, lives on the Airbus SCM and reaches the platform through the Airbus CI/CD (the AgentAiR constraint list says \"CI/CD of Airbus (Gitlab, Jenkins …) tbc\"); the spoke environments (dev / int / pro) and their project ids are unknown.",
    "legendPassages": [
      "Red frames: Agent Engine POD-only, not in the production landing zone (HR master ARD note 2026-02-27, to recheck); Gemini Enterprise planned Q4 2026, not SEC4AI-assessed; Agent Runtime under VPC-SC needs `min_instances` ≥ 1; PSL spoke template end 2026, retrofit required."
    ]
  },
